This is a sample to build the kind of database infrastructure we need for Ziniki,
i.e. a combo of neptune and dynamo dbs

    target trial_dbs

Let's create a neptune cluster.  I think this is all you need - a cluster with a name.
After that, everything else seems to be gravy.

        ensure aws.Neptune.Cluster "neptune_cluster" => neptune
            @teardown delete

And then let's create a dynamo db.  Tables are deffo per region, and at some point we
need to consider regions.

        ensure aws.DynamoDB.Table "ziids" => ziids_table
            @teardown delete
            // TODO: AttributeDefinitions
            // TODO: KeySchema // TODO: I would like to wrap this up in the attributes
            // I think that is most easily done by having a (nested) adverb @Key <hash> or @Key <range>

            // There are many more, but I don't think they are needed